  "body": "The `site` job of `release.yml` run 44976953856 (tag v0.25.0) failed on the site tests (#3271). So `pages` did not deploy, and https://neotech.github.io/Camcraft/ does not show \"CamCraft 0.25.0\". PR #3274 fixed the tests on `main` (5c8340b81). The tag does not move, so a re-run of the tag run fails again.\n\nPlan (decision recorded on #3271, comment 7073324082):\n\n1. Make a branch `site/v0.25.0`: v0.25.0 plus only the docs and test fixes of PR #3274 that apply to the 0.25.0 tree. No app code and no section for an operation that came after the tag (V-Carve).\n2. One workflow PR on `main` adds the input `site_only` to the existing `workflow_dispatch` of `release.yml`. With that input, only `site` and `pages` run, from the dispatched ref. `publish` stays tag-only. No new trigger. The decision file is `docs/decisions/3271-site-redeploy.md`.\n3. Owner ask (a settings change): add deployment branch policy `site/*` to environment github-pages (Settings > Environments > github-pages, or `gh api -X POST repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/environments/github-pages/deployment-branch-policies -f name='site/*' -f type=branch`)\n4. Dispatch once on `site/v0.25.0`. The work is done when `pages` is green and the site shows \"CamCraft 0.25.0\".\n\nFallback: if the policy is not added, the 0.25.0 site content ships with the deploy of v0.26.0, and this issue closes then.\n",
